  "id": "hatajo_de_negritos",
  "name": "Hatajo de negritos (south-central coast Christmas troupes)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The hatajos de negritos and de pallitas are Afro-Peruvian Christmas devotional troupes of Peru's south-central coast, centred on El Carmen in Chincha and inscribed by UNESCO in 2019, who sing and dance before the Christ Child from late December to the Epiphany. A violinist leads the negritos, who ring handbells and stamp zapateo footwork between their sung verses, while the pallitas are troupes of girls and young women who sing in chorus. The Ballumbrosio family of El Carmen are the tradition's best-known keepers.",
  "recipe": "classic late-2010s hatajo de negritos, ritual Devotional, Afro-diasporic branch. fiddle, handbells diatonic handbells rung handbells. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
